<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span>Performance (ACC %) with different numbers of retrieved documents per search. Retrieving 3 documents achieves the best average performance. While 5 documents shows advantages on specific datasets (MuSiQue, Bamboogle for 7B; HotpotQA, Bamboogle for 3B), the overall best configuration is 3 documents.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A6.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ F.1 Impact of Retrieved Documents per Search ‣ Appendix F Additional Results ‣ Search-P1: Path-Centric Reward Shaping for Stable and Efficient Agentic RAG Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> shows how the number of retrieved documents per search iteration affects model performance. Retrieving too few documents may miss relevant information, while retrieving too many can introduce noise and increase context length.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.2 </span>Effect of Format Reward on Output Compliance</h3>

