<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 10: </span>Effect of soft outcome scoring (ACC %). Multi-hop QA datasets benefit more from soft scoring (+3.0–3.7%) compared to general QA datasets (+1.1–1.5%), while the internal AD-QA dataset shows the largest improvement (+8.8–11.0%), confirming that complex enterprise queries benefit most from partial credit signals.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A6.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A6.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ F.6 Detailed Soft Outcome Scoring Analysis ‣ Appendix F Additional Results ‣ Search-P1: Path-Centric Reward Shaping for Stable and Efficient Agentic RAG Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> provides the per-dataset breakdown of the soft outcome scoring ablation (corresponding to Figure <a href="#S4.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 4.3.1 Format Reward ‣ 4.3 Ablation Study ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Search-P1: Path-Centric Reward Shaping for Stable and Efficient Agentic RAG Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> in the main paper).</p>
</div>
