</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 12: </span>Effect of outcome accuracy weight <math id="A6.T12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{a}</annotation></semantics></math> on performance (ACC %, Qwen2.5-7B). The optimal value is <math id="A6.T12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{a}=0.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{a}=0.6</annotation></semantics></math>, which achieves the best average performance. While <math id="A6.T12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{a}=0.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{a}=0.8</annotation></semantics></math> shows slight advantages on MuSiQue and Bamboogle, <math id="A6.T12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{a}=0.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{a}=0.6</annotation></semantics></math> provides better overall results.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A6.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Tables <a href="#A6.T11" title="Table 11 ‣ F.7 Detailed Hyperparameter Sensitivity Analysis ‣ Appendix F Additional Results ‣ Search-P1: Path-Centric Reward Shaping for Stable and Efficient Agentic RAG Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> and <a href="#A6.T12" title="Table 12 ‣ F.7 Detailed Hyperparameter Sensitivity Analysis ‣ Appendix F Additional Results ‣ Search-P1: Path-Centric Reward Shaping for Stable and Efficient Agentic RAG Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a> provide the per-dataset breakdown for hyperparameter sensitivity analysis (corresponding to Figure <a href="#S5.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ 5.1 Hyperparameter Sensitivity ‣ 5 Analysis ‣ Search-P1: Path-Centric Reward Shaping for Stable and Efficient Agentic RAG Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> in the main paper).</p>
</div>
</section>
