<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 13: </span>Detailed accuracy (%) across LLM evaluators (Qwen2.5-7B + GRPO). Qwen3-32B shows modest degradation (<math id="A6.T13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>−</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-</annotation></semantics></math>1.1 Avg.), while Qwen3-8B exhibits larger drops on multi-hop tasks where step coverage evaluation is more challenging.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A6.SS8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A6.T13" title="Table 13 ‣ F.8 Detailed LLM Evaluator Analysis ‣ Appendix F Additional Results ‣ Search-P1: Path-Centric Reward Shaping for Stable and Efficient Agentic RAG Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> provides the per-dataset breakdown for the LLM evaluator analysis. The Qwen3-8B evaluator shows larger drops on multi-hop datasets (e.g., <math id="A6.SS8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>−</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-</annotation></semantics></math>4.0 on MuSiQue, <math id="A6.SS8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>−</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-</annotation></semantics></math>4.0 on 2Wiki) where accurately counting covered reasoning steps is more challenging.</p>
</div>
